    <section>
      <h2>Map, Data, and Third-Party Sources</h2>
      <p>RRGH maps may use or reference government, public-domain, open-data, licensed, or third-party map and geographic-data sources. Source names, required credits, and license notices will be displayed with the map, route page, source panel, or other reasonably visible attribution location as appropriate. Third-party content remains subject to the rights and terms of its provider, and RRGH does not grant you rights that the provider has not granted.</p>
      <p>A link to, use of, or attribution to a government agency, map provider, land manager, or other third party does not mean that party sponsors, endorses, verifies, or guarantees RRGH or an RRGH route. RRGH does not control the continued availability, completeness, accuracy, or terms of third-party maps, services, links, or data.</p>
      <p>The Community / Informal Trails layer may display OpenStreetMap paths explicitly tagged as informal and other community-mapped path or footway candidates that do not substantially match the authoritative USDA Forest Service trail geometry used by RRGH. That comparison is a data-screening method, not a determination that a path is unofficial, maintained, open, lawful to use, or accurately mapped. OpenStreetMap data is community-maintained and may be incomplete, outdated, incorrectly tagged, difficult to follow, discouraged, restricted, private, closed, or otherwise unsuitable for travel. A community or informal path appearing on the map is not an RRGH recommendation and does not establish legal access. The route planner may snap to displayed community/informal paths unless the loaded OpenStreetMap feature is explicitly tagged private or no access; planner availability is a geometry aid and is not a statement that travel is lawful, safe, maintained, or currently open.</p>
      <p>The route planner may also snap to mapped road-centerline geometry from USDA Forest Service and Kentucky public road datasets. Road snapping is a geometry aid for planning a hike that includes road walking; it does not determine whether a road has a lawful or safe pedestrian route, shoulder, closure, traffic condition, maintenance condition, or current access. Limited-access road classes are excluded where the source classification identifies them, but users remain responsible for confirming whether walking on a particular road is lawful and appropriate.</p>
      <p>OpenStreetMap-derived information is attributed to © OpenStreetMap contributors and is subject to the Open Database License (ODbL) and the terms identified through the map attribution/source disclosure.</p>
    </section>

